```

Total throwing error sites found: **223** (225 raw matches − 2 declaration/prototype false positives).

## Section 1 — Sentinel-return / non-throwing rejections (directly callable across FFI)

These are the rejections an external `.so` caller observes as a *return value*, not a `longjmp`.

| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |
|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|
| S1 | `js_regcomp` | any pattern that hits a `die()` in `regexp.c` | returns `NULL`, `*errorp` set to the exact message string |
| S2 | `js_regcomp` | valid pattern | returns non-`NULL`, `*errorp` untouched |
| S3 | `js_regexec` | subject does not match | returns `REG_NOMATCH` (`1`) |
| S4 | `js_regexec` | recursion depth `> REG_MAXREC` (4096) during match | returns `REG_NOMATCH` (`1`) (`regexec` bails, `-1` internally mapped) |
| S5 | `js_regexec` | `eflags` = out-of-range int (e.g. `0x7fffffff`, `-1`) | only `REG_NOTBOL` (4) bit inspected; other bits ignored |
| S6 | `js_regcomp` | `cflags` = out-of-range int | only `REG_ICASE`(1)/`REG_NEWLINE`(2) bits inspected |
| S7 | `js_ploadstring` | source with a syntax error | returns `1`, error object pushed on stack |
| S8 | `js_ploadstring` | called with `J->trytop == JS_TRYLIMIT` (64) | returns `1`, pushes litstr `"exception stack overflow"` |
| S9 | `js_dostring` | source with a syntax or runtime error | returns `1`, calls report callback |
| S10 | `js_pcall` | callee throws | returns `1`, exception value on stack |
| S11 | `js_pcall` | callee is not callable | returns `1`, `TypeError: not a function` |
| S12 | `js_pconstruct` | callee is not a constructor | returns `1`, `TypeError` |
| S13 | `js_trystring` | value whose `toString` throws | returns the caller-supplied `error` pointer |
| S14 | `js_trynumber` | value whose `valueOf` throws | returns the caller-supplied `error` double |
| S15 | `js_tryinteger` | value whose `valueOf` throws | returns the caller-supplied `error` int |
| S16 | `js_tryboolean` | value whose conversion throws | returns the caller-supplied `error` int |
| S17 | `js_tryrepr` | value whose repr throws | returns the caller-supplied `error` pointer |
| S18 | `js_isuserdata` | tag does not match the object's tag | returns `0` |
| S19 | `js_isuserdata` | idx holds a non-userdata value | returns `0` |
| S20 | `js_compare` | either side is `NaN` (unordered) | `*okay = 0` |
| S21 | `js_type` | any value | returns one of `JS_ISUNDEFINED..JS_ISOBJECT`; internal types map deterministically |
| S22 | `jsU_chartorune` | truncated / malformed UTF-8 sequence | returns `1`, `*rune = Runeerror` (`0xFFFD`) |
| S23 | `jsU_chartorune` | overlong encoding | returns `1`, `*rune = Runeerror` |
| S24 | `jsU_chartorune` | surrogate-range or >`Runemax` codepoint encoding | returns `1`, `*rune = Runeerror` |
| S25 | `jsU_chartorune` | empty string (`""`) | returns `1`, `*rune = 0` |
| S26 | `jsU_runetochar` | rune `< 0` or `> Runemax` (0x10FFFF) | encodes `Runeerror` |
| S27 | `jsU_runelen` | rune out of range | returns length of `Runeerror` encoding (3) |
| S28 | `js_strtod` | no parsable number at start | returns `0`, `*end == input` |
| S29 | `js_strtod` | overflow (`1e400`) | returns `HUGE_VAL`/`inf` |
| S30 | `js_strtod` | underflow (`1e-400`) | returns `0` |
| S31 | `js_strtol` | digit(s) invalid for the given base | stops at first invalid digit |
| S32 | `js_strtol` | value out of `long` range | clamps to `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN` |
| S33 | `js_stringtofloat` | unparsable string | returns `0`, `*end == input` |
| S34 | `jsV_stringtonumber` | string that is not a valid numeric literal | returns `NaN` |
| S35 | `jsV_stringtonumber` | `""` / all-whitespace | returns `0` |
| S36 | `js_isarrayindex` | string is not a canonical array index (leading `0`, `-1`, `> 2^32-2`, non-digit) | returns `0` |
| S37 | `js_intern` | `""` | returns interned empty string (no error) |
| S38 | `js_utfptrtoidx` / `js_utflen` | malformed UTF-8 | counts `Runeerror` as one rune |
| S39 | `js_runeat` | index past end of string | returns `0` |
| S40 | `js_newstate` | `flags` with no valid bit (e.g. `0x7ffffffe`) | only `JS_STRICT`(1) bit inspected; state created |
| S41 | `js_newstate` | `alloc` callback returns `NULL` on first allocation | returns `NULL` |
