[38;5;252m[1m## Things worth knowing[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **No divergences were found in the translation.** Every failure I chased turned out to be a harness bug or genuine C behaviour: stack accounting on [38;5;10mjs_pcall[0m's error path, borrowed-pointer lifetimes ([38;5;10mjs_newcfunction[0m/[38;5;10mjs_pushliteral[0m/[38;5;10mjsB_props[0m store the pointer without copying), [38;5;10mjs_ref[0m's [38;5;10m%p[0m object addresses, and [38;5;10mnew Date()[0m reading the wall clock.[0m[0m
- **I proved the harness bites** by injecting two deliberate bugs — an off-by-one in [38;5;10mjsU_runelen[0m at [38;5;10m0x10FFFF[0m and a one-letter change to an error message — and confirming each was caught, then restoring and re-verifying by checksum.[0m[0m
